{
  "About": "The key numbers README.md and the new-user guide's walk-through (section 14) state, in one place, and the recorded |S| of every shipped run. circuitRF's tests check that each quoted value's Readme text appears in both pages, recompute the closed forms from the cells' VARs, hold the recorded Pair result to Cohn's ideal coupled line, and gate 4 (Category=Benchmark) re-runs the three shipped runs and holds every recorded |S| to its run's Tolerance (dB). Measured once on an Apple M4 (10 cores, 16 GB), macOS 27.0, Palace 0.18.1 on 10 processes, Gmsh 4.15.2, openEMS 0.37.0-rc3, OpenCASCADE 8.0.1. A time is the whole run's wall clock; memory is Palace's own peak over its processes; openEMS's size is its grid's cell count.",
